    926	### C3 — Find a non-natural correlation that breaks GUE
    927	
    928	**Question:** Construct a *bespoke* statistic on zeros — not pair, not
    929	triple, not BK — that is sensitive to prime arithmetic and is
    930	non-trivial.
    931	
    932	**Why frontier:** the published statistics (pair, n-correlation, form
    933	factor, BK) all match GUE. A statistic tailored to π(x) might break it.
    934	
    935	**Cross-domain ingredient:** information theory / hypothesis testing
    936	on statistical ensembles.
    937	
    938	**Concrete first step:** consider the statistic
    939	`S(γ_1, ..., γ_n) := Σ_p log(p) · cos(γ_i · log p)` for primes p ≤ Y.
    940	Is its empirical distribution over zero windows consistent with the
    941	GUE prediction (computable from sine-kernel)?
    942	
    943	**Failure profile:** every statistic of zeros is a linear combination
    944	of standard correlation measures, so the test reduces to one of those.
    945	
    946	**Budget:** 1-2 sessions.
