    12	- Three independent measurements that did not previously exist in the
    13	  project (PTF degree, depth-2 W=1 size, N=6 PRIMES-vs-random gap).
    14	- A clean STRUCTURAL MECHANISM (1-bit oddness advantage) that explains
    15	  the PRIMES-vs-random gap at N=6 in elementary terms.
    16	- A negative result for §A1 as literally posed (depth-5 size-2000
    17	  enumeration intractable).
    18	
    19	**Why B and not A:** the session did not produce a small explicit
    20	polylog-promising circuit for PRIMES at N=8 (which would have been the
    21	A-grade outcome). The PRIMES-vs-random gap at N=6, while statistically
    22	significant (p < 0.001), reduces to the well-known "odd primes" fact —
    23	a known elementary structure, not a new arithmetic insight.
    24	
    25	**Why not C:** the session produced 3+ artefacts not previously in the
    26	project:
    27	- Exact PTF degrees of PRIMES at N=4..8 (4 at N=8) — first measurement.
    28	- Exact depth-2 W=1 sign-threshold sizes at N=4 (3) and N=6 (6) —
    29	  first measurement.
    30	- The PRIMES-vs-random gap is the FIRST PRIMES circuit-complexity
