n-Saikia-Marrakchi-Brox-Hutter 2020 ICLR "Understanding and Robustifying DARTS"). **Adds a 36th orthogonal pseudorandomness measure** (DARTS continuous-relaxation reachable loss) with the SAME elementary mechanism as S84 (oddness-of-primes mod 2). **Mode I-with-mechanism**: the cross-domain DARTS technique survives import (the soft training does extract the parity bit) but is not load-bearing for any new conclusion — depth-2 SAT and depth-3 DARTS find the same predictor. **Falsifiers** (open follow-ups): (i) larger search (G_1, G_2 ≥ 32, depth ≥ 4) with XOR-favoured initialisation; (ii) different discretisation (top-k threshold + soft-to-hard rounding, Bender 2018); (iii) calibrated control on the same larger search space showing PRIMES-residual gap. **Cross-domain technique** Liu-Simonyan-Yang ICLR 2019 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.09055) PROPOSED → USED-I; see `CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §8`. **Reduces structurally to E1.10 / E3.13 / S84** — joins pseudorandomness-confirms-pseudorandomness closure family. Refines `novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md` with a 36th measure. See `experiments/ml/darts_primes/{darts_primes.py, baselines.py, calibrated_control.py, darts_primes_results.md, run/}`, `archive/sessions/session216_d8_darts_primes.md`. | 216 |
