    2	
    3	**Status:** Novel synthesis. Individual measures from Sessions 17-56 plus
    4	four adjacent representations (S48 Dirichlet character spectrum of chi_P;
    5	S51 regular CF of the prime constant alpha=Σ 2^{-p}; S68 Bessel-basis PSLQ
    6	identity test for f(x) = pi(x) - R(x); S57 smoothness-of-(p-1) conditioning
    7	of delta(pi(p))).
    8	No published work examines this many independent complexity measures on a single natural function.
    9	
    10	## Summary
    11	
    12	pi(x) mod 2 (and its smooth-residual companion f(x) = pi(x) - R(x)) is
    13	indistinguishable from a random Boolean / Gaussian function under every
    14	structural complexity measure tested in this project (35). This is the
    15	project's strongest collective finding.
    16	
    17	The 2 measures added in S55 (A(x) mod 2, C_3(x) mod 2) probe the COMPONENTS of
    18	the Liouville-identity decomposition pi(x) = (x - L(x))/2 - C_3(x) (E2.2). They
    19	strengthen the picture: even after splitting pi(x) mod 2 = A(x) mod 2 XOR
    20	C_3(x) mod 2, EACH of the two halves is independently pseudorandom and the
    21	two are mutually independent (I(A; C_3) ≈ 2 × 10⁻⁵ bits).  In particular
    22	A(x) mod 2 (equivalently L(x) mod 4 modulo the trivial L mod 2 = x mod 2)
    23	is *more* pseudorandom than pi(x) mod 2 itself — its only nontrivial
    24	auto-structure (sparse density bias) is removed because Omega(n) is odd for
    25	exactly half of n.
    26	
    27	The 5 measures added in S56 (#27..#31) extend the same picture to
    28	character-twisted Liouville sums L_chi(x) for all 34 non-trivial Dirichlet
    29	characters across q in {3, 5, 7, 11, 13}.  Each char twists by a different
    30	primitive d-th root of unity for d = ord(chi) in {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 10, 12}.
